  {
    "id": "cvpr26-172d9118c07b",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Overview of MergeVLA architecture. (1) To address destructive LoRA parameter interference in finetuned VLM, task masks are applied to all merged LoRA modules to selectively activate the merged parameters contributing to task-relevant responses while suppressing those that mislead other tasks.\n(2) To solve the incompatibility of action experts, the architecture is redesigned to contain only cross-attention blocks and use sigmoid \\mathrm{sigmoid} gate to preserve and rely on robust VLM features. Most blocks then can be merged except deeper blocks named expert head are left unmerged due to their task specification.\n(3) To address the setting where the task identity is unknown at inference time, a training-free test-time task router is adopted to dynamically select task-specified components by computing task relevance from VLM hidden states in the value-based subspace of the merged action expert.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2511.18810v2/model_arch_v4.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S2.F2",
      "panelIndex": 0,
      "panelCount": 1,
      "score": 32,
