      "id": "cvpr26-cad19a2921a3",
      "figure": "Figure 4",
      "caption": "Figure 4. Overview of generalist reward model. Left: Given a before-edited image and a user-edited after image After-u (“u” for “user”), we perturb the editing process to obtain a suboptimal image, After-w (“w” for “weak”). Middle: In the SFT stage,the reward model ﬁrst learns to generate metrics and then produces scalar rewards for the two input images. Right: In the RL stage, we introduce policy-guided reward training (PGRT), where the suboptimal image After-w is provided by the policy model rather than generated through perturbation. The goal of the RL stage is to assign a higher scalar reward to the user-edited (strong) image After-u.",
