  {
    "id": "cvpr26-f1d601eb2131",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Our training process is divided into two stages: the Reference Clip ( C ​ l ​ i ​ p 0 Clip_{0} ) Training Stage and Source Clip ( C ​ l ​ i ​ p n ∈ [ 1 , N − 1 ] Clip_{n\\in[1,N-1]} ) Training Stage. In Reference Clip Training Stage, anchors A 0 A_{0} are initialized by the fused point cloud from all frames of C ​ l ​ i ​ p 0 Clip_{0} . The anchors are fed into a spatio-temporal field ( S ​ T ​ F 0 STF_{0} ) to extract dynamic features, which are then concatenated with static features. They are decoded to Temporal Gaussian attributes and rendered via rasterization. In Source Clip Training Stage, we inherit the anchors, decoder and the static features from Reference Clip. Residual anchors are computed between the current and Reference Clip A 0 A_{0} . Finally, the same training pipeline as in the Reference Clip  stage is applied using the A n A_{n} conpensated with residual anchors and the newly initialized S ​ T ​ F STF .",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2604.13746v1/pipeline_high.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S2.F2",
      "panelIndex": 0,
      "panelCount": 1,
