      "id": "cvpr26-c831519372ab",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of MD2E. An image is processed by the MDE model to produce an edge map and an initial depth map. Dense depth labels are transformed into edge annotations to supervise the edge branch. A spectral-quantile estimator computes an edge score tpred, which calibrates the initial depth to metric scale. The final depth is trained with both ground-truth depth and edge prediction supervision, yielding sharp and accurate metric depth.",
